tion\":{\"ref\":\"d61\"},\"ref\":\"d61\",\"snippet\":\" ... the Central Board of Film Certification (CBFC), which initially banned it from screening for its perceived glorification of submissiveness of women through the character of the forgiving wife who is in \\\"ignoble servility\\\" to her husband. Other films starring Kapadia that year include Babbar Subhash's Pyar Ke ... \",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dimple_Kapadia\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d62\"},\"ref\":\"d62\",\"snippet\":\" ... Mary Roscoe is married to actor, Jeremy Swift, who plays her husband on the show.\\n* Keeley Hazell as Bex (season 1; guest seasons 2–3), Rupert's new girlfriend and eventual third wife.\\n* Ellie Taylor as Flo \\\"Sassy\\\" Collins, Rebecca's best friend who becomes attracted to Ted ... \",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ted_Lasso\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d63\"},\"ref\":\"d63\",\"snippet\":\" ... He became a reliable character actor (often in Westerns in which he often played the villain), but hit the big time when he was offered the role of the somewhat irascible Dr. Leonard \\\"Bones\\\" McCoy on the television series Star Trek (1966). He later reprised his role for ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.imdb.com/search/name/?birth_year=1920\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d64\"},\"ref\":\"d64\",\"snippet\":\" ... Nostromo was finally adapted for the small screen with an unrelated BBC television mini-series in 1997.\\n\\nPersonal life\\n\\nLean was a long-term resident of Limehouse, East London. His home on Narrow Street is still owned by his family.\\n\\nHis co-writer and producer, Norman Spencer, has ... \",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/David_Lean\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d65\"},\"ref\":\"d65\",\"snippet\":\" ... you could do worse than just making one of your at-home TV screens devoted to playing the Weerasethakul filmography on a loop. Really any of his films is Palme d'Or-worthy, and it's hard to see why \\\"Uncle Boonmee\\\" is any more so than \\\"Tropical ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.indiewire.com/feature/cannes-film-festival-palme-d-or-winners-movies-ranked-1202132111/\"}],\"next_step\":\"Inspect navigation; read a relevant page or change the locating clue.\",\"observation\":{\"first_delivered_source_round\":null,\"prior_deliveries\":0,\"query_key\":\"8bb4114768b444a32344e01c210e1b8946061dac9725a585fcbd1b51630219d8\",\"replay_requested\":false,\"result_fingerprint\":\"bf1e1c46557bedc16be991a5674ea89096f214b92a4207f695a750377311084d\",\"semantic_progress\":\"not_measured\"},\"query\":\"series actor husband wife plays unrelated characters on screen\",\"view\":\"full\"}]}","role":"tool","tool_call_id":"call_d8bbd1d6d8e6401f9b66c719"},{"content":"Let me reconsider the clues. The \"only one child survives\" with multiple marriages and children dying is very characteristic of Turkish dizis. Let me think about \"Diriliş: Ertuğrul\" or \"Kuruluş: Osman\" — but those are historical. The \"plays alongside real-life relative though unrelated in series\" is the key discriminator. Let me search for specific shows with this angle.","role":"assistant","tool_calls":[{"function":{"arguments":"{\"queries\": [\"Dirilis Ertugrul cast real life relatives married couples\", \"Kurulus Osman actor real life spouse sibling plays different character\", \"Turkish series actor real life wife husband different role same show\"], \"top_k\": 8}","name":"search"},"id":"call_3b8bc0426c2c471a953f9c74","index":0,"type":"function"}]},{"content":"